      "content": "Ah, the Eurostar, a magical train that whisks travelers from London to Paris faster than a mischievous goblin on a caffeine high. As for your heavy checked bags, the Eurostar's luggage policy is quite strict, much like a goblin's code of honor. Each checked bag can weigh up to 32kg (70lbs) and the dimensions must not exceed 62 linear inches (length + width + height). It's like trying to sneak a giant, clumsy goblin through a narrow dungeon door – you need to be precise!\n\nNow, regarding the check-in process at St Pancras, it's best to arrive early, like a goblin preparing for a grand heist. Aim to be there at least 3 hours before your departure to ensure you can smoothly navigate through security, much like a goblin slipping past a sleeping dragon. Remember, time is of the essence, and a well-prepared goblin never rushes. Good luck, and may your journey be as smooth as a goblin's midnight escapades!",
